  m_Name: Pharynx.001
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ModelPartDataSO
  id: Pharynx.001
  partName: Pharynx
  descriptionChunks:
  - The pharynx is a muscular passage located at the back of the throat that serves
    as a shared pathway for both the digestive and respiratory systems. It guides
    food from the oral cavity into the esophagus and channels air between the nasal
    passages and the larynx.
  - This structure plays an important role in swallowing, vocalization, and air conduction.
    Its coordinated muscular contractions ensure safe and efficient passage of food
    and air, preventing misdirection and supporting normal respiratory and digestive
    function.
